-- title:
--   Function field generation at squarefree level
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ be a natural number which is nonzero and squarefree. The conclusion is the predicate `FunctionFieldGeneration N`, which asserts: for every natural number $d$ dividing $N$ and nonzero, the Laurent series `qExpand ℚ d jq` belongs to the intermediate field $\mathbb{Q}(\mathtt{jq},\ \mathtt{qExpand}\ \mathbb{Q}\ N\ \mathtt{jq})$, i.e. to `IntermediateField.adjoin ℚ {jq, qExpand ℚ N jq}` inside the field `LaurentSeries ℚ` of Laurent series over $\mathbb{Q}$. Here `jq` is the distinguished element of `LaurentSeries ℚ` serving as the $q$-expansion of the modular invariant $j$, and for a nonzero $m$ the map `qExpand ℚ m` is the ring endomorphism of `LaurentSeries ℚ` obtained by transporting the Hahn-series support along multiplication by $m$ on exponents, that is, the substitution $q \mapsto q^{m}$. Thus for squarefree $N$ each $j(q^{d})$ with $d \mid N$ lies in the subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by $j(q)$ and $j(q^{N})$.
--
--   This is the statement that, at squarefree level, the field generated by all $j(q^{d})$ for $d \mid N$ collapses to the two-generator field $\mathbb{Q}(j(q), j(q^{N}))$, the $q$-expansion model of the function field of $X_0(N)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$. It is used in the purely algebraic determination of $[\mathbb{Q}(j)(j_N):\mathbb{Q}(j)] = \psi(N)$ and the irreducibility of the modular polynomial, and is cited by [`ModularCurve.jqN_prime_not_mem_full`](thm.html#ModularCurve.jqN_prime_not_mem_full) and [`ModularCurve.minpoly_jqN_map_eq_prod_slots`](thm.html#ModularCurve.minpoly_jqN_map_eq_prod_slots).
